},{"name":"Michaelia Cash","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10707","person_slug":"michaelia-cash","vote":"no"},{"name":"Mitch Fifield","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10224","person_slug":"mitch-fifield","vote":"no"},{"name":"Penny Wright","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10765","person_slug":"penny-wright","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Peter Whish-Wilson","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10780","person_slug":"peter-whish-wilson","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Rachel Siewert","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10584","person_slug":"rachel-siewert","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Richard Colbeck","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10131","person_slug":"richard-colbeck","vote":"no"},{"name":"Richard Di Natale","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10755","person_slug":"richard-di-natale","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sarah Hanson-Young","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10711","person_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Scott Ludlam","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10713","person_slug":"scott-ludlam","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sean Edwards","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10756","person_slug":"sean-edwards","vote":"no"},{"name":"Simon Birmingham","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10044","person_slug":"simon-birmingham","vote":"no"},{"name":"Stephen Parry","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10507","person_slug":"stephen-parry","vote":"no"},{"name":"Trish Crossin","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10161","person_slug":"trish-crossin","vote":"no"},{"name":"Ursula Stephens","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10609","person_slug":"ursula-stephens","vote":"no"}],"name":"Motions - Coal Seam Gas - Protect rivers, groundwater, agriculatural lands and natural environment","noes":39,"question":"The majority voted against a [motion](http://www.openaustralia.org/senate/?id=2013-02-28.31.1) introduced by Greens Senator [Larissa Waters](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/mp.php?mpn=Larissa_Waters&mpc=Senate&house=senate). This means that the motion was rejected. The motion was: _That the Senate-_ _(a) notes that:_ _(i) [coal seam gas](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coal_seam_gas) is a high-risk industry that poses unacceptable risks to our rivers and [groundwater](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Groundwater), agricultural lands and natural environment, and our communities, and_(Read more about coal seam gas [here](http://www.abc.net.au/news/specials/coal-seam-gas-by-the-numbers/).) _(ii) since becoming Australia's Minister for Sustainability, Environment, Water, Population and Communities, [Mr Burke](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/mp.php?mpn=Tony_Burke&mpc=Watson&house=representatives) has not rejected a single coal seam gas project, rather approved multiple enormous coal seam gas field developments across [Queensland](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Queensland), and most recently in [Gloucester](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gloucester,_New_South_Wales) in [New South Wales](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_South_Wales) despite significant community concerns about the health and environmental impacts of this new industry; and_ _(b) calls on the Federal Government to protect Australia's rivers and groundwater, agricultural lands and natural environment, our communities and the world's climate and stop this new high-risk industry._ References","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-61","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2013-02-28/2"}
